 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 505 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of an occupancy tax in the village of Tuckahoe, in relation\nto extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5082",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5082-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 505 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5082\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 505 of the laws of 2016,\namending the tax law relating to the imposition of an occupancy tax in\nthe village of Tuckahoe, in relation to extending the effectiveness\nthereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the expiration date of chapter 505 of the laws of 2016, which\nauthorizes the Village of Tuckahoe to enact a room occupancy tax not to\nexceed 3%.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe expiration date of section 1202-z-1 of the tax law, as enacted by\nchapter 505 of the laws of 2016, authorizing the Village of Tuckahoe to\nenact a room occupancy tax not exceeding 3%, is extended to September 1,\n2022.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 505 of the laws of 2016 granted the Village of Tuckahoe the\nability to impose a 3% daily room tax on any room in a hotel, motel, or\nsimilar place of public accommodation. This tax has helped raise reven-\nues to support municipal expenses. The law is set to expire on September\n1, 2019 and this legislation will extend the expiration date to Septem-\nber 1, 2022.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA. 9690/ S.7153 of 2016 was signed, chapter 505.\nA.82 of 2015, same as S.564, Veto No. 307.\nA.9626 of 2014, passed the Assembly.\nSame as S.7316 of 2014, referred to investigations and governmental\noperations.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed September 1, 2022.\n",
